    "label": "Horizontal Resistance Line",
    "category": "momentum",
    "description": "The most recent swing-high pivot whose close has never been exceeded since — a wick through it is fine, only a closing print above breaks the line. When an older unbroken pivot sits within \"Same-ceiling tolerance\" of that newest one, it is treated as the same ceiling and the line is dated to the older touch, not the newest one — most published resistance lines are dated from an earlier retest, not the latest. Base length/depth bound how old and how wide the base under that ceiling may be, \"Max % below line\" requires price to still be pressing it rather than sitting far under an old, technically-unbroken high, and \"Max % below 20 EMA\" requires price not to have drifted away from its own short-term trend.",
    "parameters": [
      {
        "id": "lookbackDays",
        "label": "Search window",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 252,
        "unit": "d"
      },
      {
        "id": "minSwingPct",
        "label": "Swing noise floor",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 1.5,
        "unit": "%"
      },
      {
        "id": "clusterTolerancePct",
        "label": "Same-ceiling tolerance",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 2.5,
        "unit": "%"
      },
      {
        "id": "minBaseLengthDays",
        "label": "Min base length",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 15,
        "unit": "d"
      },
      {
        "id": "maxBaseLengthDays",
        "label": "Max base length",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 400,
        "unit": "d"
      },
      {
        "id": "minBaseDepthPct",
        "label": "Min base depth",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 0,
        "unit": "%"
      },
      {
        "id": "maxBaseDepthPct",
        "label": "Max base depth",
        "type": "number",
        "defaultValue": 60,
        "unit": "%"
      },
      {
        "id": "maxPctBelowLine",
